            "charspan": [
              658,
              734
            ]
          }
        ],
        "orig": "Unlike in standard RL setups, the reward assigned to a given action in our setting depends on the model parameters θ at the time the action is taken (since θ is updated to θ ′ , which is then evaluated). As a result, the underlying RL state must include the policy's parameters and is given by ( C, θ ) , even though the policy's observation is limited to C (placing θ directly in context is infeasible). The implication of this is that (state, action, reward) triples collected with a previous version of the model, θ old, may become stale and misaligned for the current model θ current. For this reason, we adopt an on-policy approach, in which self-edits Algorithm 1 Self-Adapting LLMs (SEAL): Self-Edit Reinforcement Learning Loop",
        "text": "Unlike in standard RL setups, the reward assigned to a given action in our setting depends on the model parameters θ at the time the action is taken (since θ is updated to θ ′ , which is then evaluated). As a result, the underlying RL state must include the policy's parameters and is given by ( C, θ ) , even though the policy's observation is limited to C (placing θ directly in context is infeasible). The implication of this is that (state, action, reward) triples collected with a previous version of the model, θ old, may become stale and misaligned for the current model θ current. For this reason, we adopt an on-policy approach, in which self-edits Algorithm 1 Self-Adapting LLMs (SEAL): Self-Edit Reinforcement Learning Loop"
      }
